1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,840
Why is the cure for the curse here?

2
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:05,200
<i>Once the curse is lifted,</i>

3
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:08,840
<i>the cursed person will lose</i>
<i>all memories of the curser,</i>

4
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:10,560
<i>as if they never knew each other.</i>

5
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:12,760
<i>Your birthday is on the final day.</i>

6
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:15,200
<i>I want us to share a memory that day.</i>

7
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:16,600
<i>I'm sorry, Khobfa.</i>

8
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:20,520
<i>I just want to stay</i>
<i>in your memories a little longer.</i>

9
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:22,000
Just one more week.

10
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:23,800
I'm excited.

11
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:25,560
Excited about what?

12
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:29,440
The band competition, obviously.

13
00:00:30,920 --> 00:00:32,280
Are you happy?

14
00:00:34,520 --> 00:00:37,720
Yeah. I'm really happy.

15
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:40,680
What about you? Are you happy?

16
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:46,040
Just seeing you do
what you love makes me happy.

17
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:55,920
Take that.

18
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:07,640
Thank you for always believing in me.

19
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:24,520
Hey!

20
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:27,800
I'm going to sleep.

21
00:01:33,080 --> 00:01:37,240
Thanks for having the courage
to open your heart again too.

22
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:47,280
Hey!

23
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:49,400
Whoa.

24
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:51,720
You're taking advantage of me, huh?

25
00:01:57,520 --> 00:02:01,360
Hey, enough. Go to sleep.

26
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:03,600
Sleep already.

27
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:07,680
There you go again.

28
00:02:08,199 --> 00:02:11,000
Go sleep on your own pillow.
Go. Move over.

29
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:12,400
I just want to sleep close to you.

30
00:02:12,480 --> 00:02:13,840
Isn't this close enough?

31
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:14,440
All right, everyone.

32
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:17,640
Go ahead and practice, okay?
Make it look cool.

33
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:20,840
I'll record and send this to the seniors
for the final rehearsal.

34
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:21,800
Sure.

35
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:23,920
- Ready?
- Let's go.

36
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:26,120
One, two, three.

37
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:29,720
<i>Wake up to the same old things</i>

38
00:03:30,720 --> 00:03:33,840
<i>And the world is never kind</i>

39
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:38,320
<i>Feels like I did some wrong things</i>

40
00:03:51,880 --> 00:03:53,400
Hey, guys. It's okay.

41
00:03:53,480 --> 00:03:55,920
Don't be tense. We can do this.

42
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,360
Let's try again.

43
00:03:58,160 --> 00:04:01,600
Tell you what.
I'll play and sing the chorus first.

44
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:03,960
Then you guys join in, okay?

45
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:05,760
- Yeah.
- Okay.

46
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:16,079
<i>Maybe I'm a man who is so unlucky</i>

47
00:04:16,160 --> 00:04:20,279
<i>Like I've been cursed</i>
<i>And everything gets messy</i>

48
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:23,040
<i>Whatever I do ends in heartache</i>

49
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:26,880
<i>Disappointment is my only friend</i>

50
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:31,880
<i>But there's still one thing</i>
<i>That somehow turned out right</i>

51
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:35,640
<i>Whatever comes,</i>
<i>I know you'll be there by my side</i>

52
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:39,600
<i>No matter how unlucky life may be…</i>

53
00:04:46,360 --> 00:04:47,680
Where the hell is it, Dan?

54
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:50,000
I'm sorry, Rin.

55
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:58,880
Hey, guys.

56
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:01,880
The final competition is only a week away.

57
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:04,640
Have some confidence. We can do this.

58
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:08,320
Think about the prize money.
A hundred thousand baht.

59
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:09,800
A hundred thousand!

60
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:25,280
Hey, I'll go get us some more snacks.

61
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:27,560
But we've still got loads left.

62
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:31,080
Yeah, we haven't even finished
what you bought last time.

63
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:34,400
You guys need to keep your energy up.

64
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:36,880
You're practicing so hard.
That takes energy.

65
00:05:36,960 --> 00:05:38,680
I'll go get some more.

66
00:05:46,960 --> 00:05:49,680
Guys, I need your advice.

67
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:06,360
Please let everyone in Khobfa's band
play well and win the final competition.

68
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:10,440
If our band wins,
we'll come play live for you.

69
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:14,360
Amen.

70
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:21,680
Amen!

71
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:24,240
What? You're going to ask Rin out?

72
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:26,600
Yeah.

73
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:28,880
Wait, aren't you two already together?

74
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:31,280
Yeah, I thought
you made it official ages ago.

75
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:35,440
No. We're still in the talking stage.

76
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:37,360
But you sleep next to each other
every night?

77
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:39,080
You're basically boyfriends already.

78
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:42,560
That's why I'm asking you guys.

79
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:46,000
Hey.

80
00:06:48,840 --> 00:06:51,520
I really want to make things
official with Rin.

81
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:57,480
Do you think I should ask him
to be my boyfriend?

82
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:59,960
Ask yourself if you're ready first.

83
00:07:01,200 --> 00:07:04,440
But I think Rin likes you too.

84
00:07:04,520 --> 00:07:08,160
Yeah. You'll never know unless you try.

85
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:14,000
So what do you guys think I should do?

86
00:07:15,680 --> 00:07:16,760
What are you guys doing?

87
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:17,840
Huh?

88
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:19,280
We were talking about practice!

89
00:07:19,360 --> 00:07:20,960
We were talking about practice.

90
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:24,160
We were just discussing what to do
at our next practice, right?

91
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:25,640
- Yeah, that's right.
- Yeah.

92
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:27,400
Why'd you buy so much stuff?

93
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:28,960
Yeah, seriously.

94
00:07:29,040 --> 00:07:30,360
- Whoa.
- Look, Danthai.

95
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:32,520
Why'd you buy so much red soda?

96
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:34,760
Are they for God offering or something?

97
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:40,760
<i>It's still only you, as it's always been</i>

98
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:45,320
<i>It's only you and it'll forever be</i>

99
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:46,760
What do you think of this song?

100
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:48,840
Yeah, it sounds good.

101
00:07:48,920 --> 00:07:51,040
Hey!

102
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:53,920
You two make such a good couple.

103
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,480
What? You guys never stop teasing us.

104
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:58,440
Can't help it. You're too cute together.

105
00:07:58,520 --> 00:08:00,600
Aww!

106
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:06,120
DAD

107
00:08:10,280 --> 00:08:11,640
DAD

108
00:08:16,680 --> 00:08:19,680
So, is this song okay?

109
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:24,360
It's good, but shouldn't you ask
the rest of the band?

110
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:27,600
Hey, what do you guys think?

111
00:08:27,680 --> 00:08:29,080
- It's fab!
- It's fab!

112
00:08:31,080 --> 00:08:33,720
DAD

113
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:39,760
You should answer.
He might need something.

114
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,480
What is it, Dad?

115
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,640
I'm fine staying here.

116
00:08:56,720 --> 00:08:58,360
We know each other well.

117
00:08:58,440 --> 00:09:00,520
Mochi's been my friend since high school.

118
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:04,280
Mochi took care of me
when things were even harder.

119
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:07,720
Why, Dad?

120
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:10,720
Why does loving someone
have to be so damn complicated?

121
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:12,360
No matter what you say,

122
00:09:12,880 --> 00:09:14,720
I want to stay with Mochi.

123
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:16,160
I'm hanging up, Dad.

124
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:37,720
Thank you.

125
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:55,920
Talking to the plant?

126
00:09:57,880 --> 00:09:59,560
You can talk to its owner too.

127
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:01,800
It's wilting again.

128
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:05,280
I wonder why.

129
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:10,920
GRANDMA

130
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:13,280
Hello, Grandma?

131
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:15,400
<i>It's all your fault, Khobfa!</i>

132
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:18,800
<i>Grandma fell and got hurt</i>
<i>because of you, you damn jinx!</i>

133
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:23,120
Why do you always
make life so hard for everyone?

134
00:10:24,160 --> 00:10:26,280
Stay away from Grandma from now on.
Understand?

135
00:10:26,880 --> 00:10:30,680
<i>Don't let me catch you here again,</i>
<i>or you're done for.</i>

136
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:36,080
Is something wrong?

137
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:42,480
Grandma fell.

138
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:46,400
My uncle just called.

139
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:48,880
He said it was my fault.

140
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:53,840
Khobfa, listen to me.

141
00:10:55,520 --> 00:10:59,480
It was an accident.
It wasn't your fault at all.

142
00:10:59,560 --> 00:11:00,640
Okay?

143
00:11:26,840 --> 00:11:28,720
I love being with you like this.

144
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:32,240
It feels like
we're the only ones in the world.

145
00:11:36,560 --> 00:11:37,920
Aren't you a little dramatic?

146
00:11:38,680 --> 00:11:39,720
I mean it.

147
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:43,320
I want to be with you forever.

148
00:11:44,320 --> 00:11:47,040
How do you know you'll be with me forever?

149
00:12:00,560 --> 00:12:02,120
Just allow me to.

150
00:12:04,520 --> 00:12:06,160
I'm waiting to be more than "F."

151
00:13:00,560 --> 00:13:02,080
<i>You're a jinx.</i>

152
00:13:02,160 --> 00:13:03,320
<i>It's all your fault, Khobfa!</i>

153
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:06,880
<i>Grandma got hurt because of you,</i>
<i>you damn jinx!</i>

154
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:08,560
<i>Everyone in this family died</i>
<i>because of you.</i>

155
00:13:08,640 --> 00:13:10,440
<i>- Why didn't you die instead, Khobfa?</i>
- Hey.

156
00:13:10,520 --> 00:13:13,520
Khobfa, are you sure you're okay?

157
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:15,640
You can take a break if you need to.

158
00:13:15,720 --> 00:13:18,120
Yeah, Khobfa.
Don't push yourself if you're not okay.

159
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:21,000
Right. I think we should take a break.

160
00:13:21,080 --> 00:13:23,200
No. Let me try again.

161
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:30,400
Okay. Come on.

162
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:32,040
Yeah. Try again.

163
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:39,720
You should stop bringing bad luck
to your friends, Khobfa.

164
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:42,160
<i>The band broke up because of you.</i>
<i>You know that, right?</i>

165
00:13:42,240 --> 00:13:43,480
<i>You're a jinx.</i>

166
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:46,120
<i>Grandma fell and got hurt</i>
<i>because of you, you damn jinx!</i>

167
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:50,000
<i>Everyone in this family died</i>
<i>because of you.</i>

168
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:52,240
<i>Why didn't you die instead, Khobfa?</i>

169
00:13:53,880 --> 00:13:54,760
Hey, Khobfa!

170
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:56,240
Khobfa!

171
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:57,480
- Khobfa!
- Khobfa!

172
00:13:57,560 --> 00:13:59,200
- Khobfa!
- Khobfa!

173
00:14:00,280 --> 00:14:01,240
Khobfa!

174
00:14:19,520 --> 00:14:20,920
Be honest with me, Rin.

175
00:14:21,520 --> 00:14:22,600
What the hell happened?

176
00:14:22,680 --> 00:14:24,880
Does Khobfa have a medical condition?

177
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:27,840
If you know something, tell us right now.

178
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:29,280
Well…

179
00:14:30,840 --> 00:14:36,880
Khobfa's uncle called today
and said his grandma fell.

180
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:40,320
He blamed Khobfa for it,
saying he was a jinx.

181
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:41,560
- Huh?
- Huh?

182
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:44,320
What do you mean? I don't get it.

183
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:46,200
Because…

184
00:15:00,280 --> 00:15:06,080
Rin, you know you can always
tell us anything, right?

185
00:15:06,160 --> 00:15:07,600
Yeah, Rin.

186
00:15:07,680 --> 00:15:09,560
You can trust us.

187
00:15:14,400 --> 00:15:17,440
<i>If it weren't for that curse,</i>
<i>I wouldn't be here with him today.</i>

188
00:15:18,040 --> 00:15:19,520
I feel so damn guilty.

189
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:20,920
- Shit!
- Shit!

190
00:15:21,560 --> 00:15:22,760
Is this for real?

191
00:15:22,840 --> 00:15:24,120
You cursed the wrong person?

192
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:25,840
Then why don't you lift the curse?

193
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:29,120
Yeah, Rin. Lift it.

194
00:15:32,120 --> 00:15:33,880
If I lift the curse,

195
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:35,920
Khobfa will…

196
00:15:37,800 --> 00:15:40,600
lose every memory of me.

197
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:42,600
- Huh?
- Shit.

198
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:48,160
Or should I lift the curse?

199
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:49,600
- You should.
- You should.

200
00:15:49,680 --> 00:15:51,560
Shouldn't you ask Khobfa first?

201
00:15:51,640 --> 00:15:55,040
Those memories don't just belong to you.

202
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:56,840
They're his memories too.

203
00:16:00,280 --> 00:16:04,080
Starting over
with the same person isn't easy.

204
00:16:04,680 --> 00:16:09,640
Honestly, the reason I pushed Khobfa
to enter the band competition

205
00:16:12,560 --> 00:16:14,640
was that I wanted to see him win for once.

206
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:20,680
At least he would know
he could succeed at something.

207
00:16:24,960 --> 00:16:26,280
Then he'd…

208
00:16:27,560 --> 00:16:29,520
finally stop thinking he's a jinx.

209
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:37,360
You guys have to help me.

210
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:02,760
What are you looking at?

211
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:06,640
Why'd you put it away so fast?

212
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:09,560
It's nothing.

213
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:11,480
I was just finishing up
a chat with a client.

214
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:18,359
Hey, I'm excited.

215
00:17:18,440 --> 00:17:20,079
The final round is coming up.

216
00:17:21,400 --> 00:17:24,000
You're good, Krit. You've got this.

217
00:17:27,119 --> 00:17:28,040
Thanks.

218
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:45,280
<i>Feeling any better?</i>

219
00:17:46,880 --> 00:17:51,280
Getting some fresh air
should help clear your head.

220
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:56,240
Thanks for keeping me company.

221
00:17:57,560 --> 00:17:59,560
What happened earlier?

222
00:18:01,680 --> 00:18:03,720
Were you worried about your grandma?

223
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:09,840
I've had it drilled into my head

224
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:12,760
that I'd never amount to anything.

225
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:17,360
And now Grandma got hurt because of me.

226
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:22,240
Maybe my uncle's right about me.

227
00:18:25,400 --> 00:18:29,320
When will this damn bad luck
finally go away?

228
00:18:32,280 --> 00:18:34,760
I don't want anyone else
to suffer because of me.

229
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:40,880
Khobfa.

230
00:18:43,120 --> 00:18:44,000
What if…

231
00:18:45,640 --> 00:18:49,440
I could make you lucky

232
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:53,200
and give you the perfect life
you've always wanted?

233
00:18:53,280 --> 00:18:54,960
No more bad luck.

234
00:18:55,040 --> 00:18:56,920
But it would mean losing me.

235
00:18:58,560 --> 00:19:00,200
Would you take it?

236
00:19:00,280 --> 00:19:01,280
No.

237
00:19:01,880 --> 00:19:03,600
Hey, at least think about it.

238
00:19:04,200 --> 00:19:08,440
This is your chance to stop being a jinx.

239
00:19:09,120 --> 00:19:11,480
How could I live without you?

240
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:20,200
You'll be fine.

241
00:19:22,800 --> 00:19:25,400
You won't be the old Khobfa anymore.

242
00:19:26,880 --> 00:19:28,080
You'll be a great musician.

243
00:19:28,160 --> 00:19:29,520
You have a band

244
00:19:30,680 --> 00:19:31,760
and friends.

245
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:35,120
Even without me…

246
00:19:42,040 --> 00:19:44,720
you can make your own luck now.

247
00:19:55,960 --> 00:19:58,280
If being lucky means

248
00:19:59,560 --> 00:20:01,440
not having you by my side,

249
00:20:03,080 --> 00:20:04,800
then how the hell is that lucky?

250
00:20:16,480 --> 00:20:18,240
<i>Here's the melody I just revised.</i>

251
00:20:19,040 --> 00:20:21,320
Follow along with the sheet music.

252
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:24,000
Let's work on the melody first.
I'll add the lyrics later.

253
00:20:24,080 --> 00:20:26,440
- You've got this.
- Yeah. Leave it to us.

254
00:20:31,920 --> 00:20:33,840
Come on. Where should we start?

255
00:20:35,680 --> 00:20:37,720
Our band is getting in sync.

256
00:20:37,800 --> 00:20:41,840
If this keeps up,
we'll do great in the final round.

257
00:20:43,040 --> 00:20:46,080
Yeah. Well done, Mr. President.

258
00:20:47,480 --> 00:20:51,440
Hey, when will the lyrics be ready?

259
00:20:51,520 --> 00:20:52,760
Give me a bit more time.

260
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:55,560
I'm working on them.
They'll be ready soon.

261
00:20:55,640 --> 00:20:57,560
I'm really putting my heart
into this song.

262
00:21:34,200 --> 00:21:36,480
Whoa!

263
00:21:37,120 --> 00:21:38,640
Great job.

264
00:21:38,720 --> 00:21:40,080
Amazing, everyone!

265
00:21:40,160 --> 00:21:41,840
You guys are amazing!

266
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:45,920
Tell you what. What do you want to eat?
Dan and I will go get some snacks.

267
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,280
Anything. Just pay for me.

268
00:21:48,880 --> 00:21:50,200
Same here.

269
00:21:50,280 --> 00:21:52,640
Seriously, you guys.

270
00:21:52,720 --> 00:21:55,200
What about you, Khobfa? Anything?

271
00:21:55,280 --> 00:21:58,600
I'll have whatever Rin's having.
Whatever he gets, I'll get that too.

272
00:21:58,680 --> 00:22:01,960
Wow.

273
00:22:02,040 --> 00:22:05,080
We'll get going, then. Be right back.

274
00:22:05,160 --> 00:22:07,760
- Okay. Hurry back.
- Okay.

275
00:22:10,720 --> 00:22:14,360
Ohm, Jinnie. I need to discuss something.

276
00:22:15,920 --> 00:22:16,760
Yeah? What's up?

277
00:22:16,840 --> 00:22:17,960
What is it?

278
00:22:18,040 --> 00:22:20,320
Remember what I asked you?

279
00:22:22,480 --> 00:22:24,240
About asking Rin to be my boyfriend?

280
00:22:26,400 --> 00:22:27,400
Yeah. What about it?

281
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:30,240
I've never done anything
like this in my life.

282
00:22:31,000 --> 00:22:32,520
I don't know what to do.

283
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:38,760
You two are his close friends.
Help me come up with a plan.

284
00:22:51,720 --> 00:22:53,000
<i>Krit, where are you?</i>

285
00:22:53,080 --> 00:22:54,560
<i>I need your advice.</i>

286
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:55,920
<i>Can you come see me?</i>

287
00:22:59,360 --> 00:23:02,240
RIN

288
00:23:07,520 --> 00:23:08,480
Hello?

289
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:10,600
Is something wrong, Rin?

290
00:23:14,200 --> 00:23:15,040
Rin.

291
00:23:16,880 --> 00:23:18,680
What did you need me for?

292
00:23:19,280 --> 00:23:22,120
The domain you set up for me has expired.

293
00:23:22,200 --> 00:23:25,080
I've qualified for
an international art competition.

294
00:23:25,160 --> 00:23:28,320
But I need to put my portfolio together
and send in my profile today.

295
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:29,520
Can you help me?

296
00:23:34,720 --> 00:23:36,920
<i>Okay. I've renewed it for you.</i>

297
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:38,400
You're all set for a long time.

298
00:23:39,280 --> 00:23:40,280
Thanks.

299
00:23:40,960 --> 00:23:43,240
I'll get going, then.

300
00:23:43,320 --> 00:23:44,640
Wait, Krit.

301
00:23:51,120 --> 00:23:52,120
Thank you.

302
00:23:55,040 --> 00:23:56,600
Thank you for everything.

303
00:24:01,720 --> 00:24:05,840
I'm sorry for everything too.

304
00:24:10,720 --> 00:24:12,680
For not taking better care of you.

305
00:24:13,200 --> 00:24:14,920
I owe you an apology too.

306
00:24:16,560 --> 00:24:21,720
I kept deciding everything for us
without considering your feelings.

307
00:24:27,200 --> 00:24:30,000
But seeing you happy with Mochi now…

308
00:24:30,920 --> 00:24:32,480
I'm happy for you.

309
00:24:36,480 --> 00:24:37,440
You too, Rin.

310
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:42,280
Good luck.

311
00:25:28,640 --> 00:25:31,840
<i>I'm the reason</i>
<i>Khobfa keeps having bad luck.</i>

312
00:25:32,400 --> 00:25:37,240
If it weren't for that curse,
I wouldn't be here with him today.

313
00:25:48,560 --> 00:25:49,600
What's up?

314
00:26:04,200 --> 00:26:07,920
Oh, nothing.

315
00:26:08,840 --> 00:26:12,440
I just wanted to ask about your band.

316
00:26:12,520 --> 00:26:13,760
How's practice going?

317
00:26:14,600 --> 00:26:16,160
Why do you ask?

318
00:26:16,240 --> 00:26:17,960
I'm looking forward to seeing you play.

319
00:26:18,920 --> 00:26:20,200
Just wait and see.

320
00:26:20,280 --> 00:26:22,840
I'll look forward to it, then.

321
00:26:42,640 --> 00:26:46,320
<i>Wake up…</i>

322
00:26:57,840 --> 00:26:59,080
"Wake up…"

323
00:27:00,520 --> 00:27:03,040
"Step out with the wrong foot
and fall down a drain!"

324
00:27:03,120 --> 00:27:04,000
How's that?

325
00:27:04,080 --> 00:27:05,120
What the hell is that?

326
00:27:06,080 --> 00:27:06,960
How about this?

327
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:11,480
<i>Wake up to the same old things</i>

328
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:15,920
<i>And the world is never kind</i>

329
00:27:16,480 --> 00:27:20,080
<i>Feels like I did some wrong things</i>

330
00:27:20,160 --> 00:27:24,400
<i>Even heaven's not on my side</i>

331
00:27:25,200 --> 00:27:26,040
Sounds good?

332
00:27:26,120 --> 00:27:28,800
Hey, that works.

333
00:27:28,880 --> 00:27:30,480
Keep going.

334
00:27:30,560 --> 00:27:34,520
<i>Maybe I'm a man who is so unlucky</i>

335
00:27:34,600 --> 00:27:38,720
<i>Like I've been cursed</i>
<i>And everything gets messy</i>

336
00:27:38,800 --> 00:27:40,320
<i>Whatever I do…</i>

337
00:27:40,400 --> 00:27:42,040
<i>Once the curse is lifted,</i>

338
00:27:42,120 --> 00:27:46,040
<i>the cursed person will lose</i>
<i>all memories of the curser,</i>

339
00:27:46,640 --> 00:27:48,600
<i>as if they never knew each other.</i>

340
00:27:49,280 --> 00:27:50,320
<i>What if…</i>

341
00:27:50,400 --> 00:27:54,160
<i>I could make you lucky?</i>

342
00:27:54,920 --> 00:27:56,840
<i>But it would mean losing me.</i>

343
00:27:58,400 --> 00:27:59,520
<i>Would you take it?</i>

344
00:28:00,760 --> 00:28:01,640
<i>No.</i>

345
00:28:03,240 --> 00:28:05,720
<i>How could I live without you?</i>

346
00:28:07,560 --> 00:28:09,520
How was that? Sounds good?

347
00:28:12,440 --> 00:28:14,080
Yeah, it sounds good.

348
00:28:17,200 --> 00:28:18,240
Huh?

349
00:28:18,840 --> 00:28:19,800
What's this?

350
00:28:20,960 --> 00:28:21,800
Holy shit!

351
00:28:22,320 --> 00:28:23,160
Gold!

352
00:28:25,040 --> 00:28:27,040
It's real gold!

353
00:28:28,680 --> 00:28:29,760
Surprise.

354
00:28:29,840 --> 00:28:31,360
A gift for my talented artist.

355
00:28:32,720 --> 00:28:38,360
Congrats on qualifying
for the international art competition.

356
00:28:38,440 --> 00:28:39,960
Great job.

357
00:28:41,520 --> 00:28:43,600
I've thought this through.

358
00:28:44,200 --> 00:28:46,840
Gold is an asset
that tends to hold its value.

359
00:28:47,560 --> 00:28:49,960
Keep it,
and it'll always be worth something.

360
00:28:52,760 --> 00:28:54,880
What does gold have to do with me?

361
00:28:54,960 --> 00:28:58,440
I want to invest in someone I like
for the long haul.

362
00:29:00,640 --> 00:29:06,120
Gold prices may rise and fall
with the market,

363
00:29:07,360 --> 00:29:11,920
but my feelings for you are 100% stable.

364
00:29:17,680 --> 00:29:19,400
You're so dramatic.

365
00:29:19,480 --> 00:29:20,840
I mean it.

366
00:29:20,920 --> 00:29:26,120
If gold ever hits
a hundred thousand dollars,

367
00:29:27,720 --> 00:29:31,840
I hope you'll still be by my side.

368
00:29:38,440 --> 00:29:39,400
Yeah.

369
00:29:41,400 --> 00:29:43,800
How'd you know I qualified, anyway?

370
00:29:43,880 --> 00:29:45,880
Prof. James only told me this evening.

371
00:29:50,680 --> 00:29:51,880
Of course I know.

372
00:29:52,560 --> 00:29:55,280
Ohm, Jinnie, and Danthai all knew.

373
00:29:56,080 --> 00:29:59,440
I was the last one to find out.

374
00:30:03,080 --> 00:30:06,480
Aww. There, there.

375
00:30:06,560 --> 00:30:08,440
I was going to tell you.

376
00:30:08,520 --> 00:30:10,920
I just wanted to wait until I won
and tell you all at once.

377
00:30:11,560 --> 00:30:15,760
You've been busy writing your song,
so I didn't tell you.

378
00:30:16,360 --> 00:30:18,400
You never asked either.

379
00:30:23,640 --> 00:30:25,280
Then let me ask you now.

380
00:30:27,840 --> 00:30:30,280
Is there anything else
you haven't told me?

381
00:30:31,720 --> 00:30:34,720
I want to know everything about you.

382
00:30:34,800 --> 00:30:37,920
I've told you everything about me.

383
00:30:39,280 --> 00:30:41,040
I haven't hidden anything.

384
00:30:43,200 --> 00:30:45,040
Are you hiding anything else from me?

385
00:30:46,760 --> 00:30:48,080
<i>Why did you hide it from me?</i>

386
00:30:48,160 --> 00:30:50,840
<i>A presto amora!</i>

387
00:30:50,920 --> 00:30:51,880
…LOSE ALL MEMORIES…

388
00:30:57,400 --> 00:30:58,960
<i>I'm sorry, Khobfa.</i>

389
00:31:09,720 --> 00:31:11,760
<i>Are you worried about Khobfa?</i>

390
00:31:13,360 --> 00:31:14,200
Yeah.

391
00:31:14,920 --> 00:31:18,320
Something's still weighing on me.

392
00:31:19,040 --> 00:31:22,320
Have you told him yet?
About lifting the curse?

393
00:31:26,160 --> 00:31:27,120
Not yet.

394
00:31:28,320 --> 00:31:32,720
I'm afraid he won't be able
to handle losing me.

395
00:31:34,600 --> 00:31:37,680
Aren't you the one who's scared?

396
00:31:40,080 --> 00:31:43,400
You're scared that lifting the curse

397
00:31:43,480 --> 00:31:47,200
will mean losing Khobfa, aren't you?

398
00:31:49,200 --> 00:31:51,880
You're afraid he'll look at you
and see a stranger, right?

399
00:32:02,440 --> 00:32:03,280
Excuse me.

400
00:32:04,120 --> 00:32:06,240
Here's the Winner's introduction video.

401
00:32:18,640 --> 00:32:21,240
THE WINNER'S INTRODUCTION

402
00:32:25,160 --> 00:32:28,200
<i>I'm the reason</i>
<i>Khobfa keeps having bad luck.</i>

403
00:32:28,280 --> 00:32:32,560
<i>If it weren't for that curse,</i>
<i>I wouldn't be here with him today.</i>

404
00:32:34,080 --> 00:32:35,920
- The Winner, right?
- Yes.

405
00:32:36,000 --> 00:32:37,640
I'll put it on to promote your band.

406
00:32:37,720 --> 00:32:40,480
- Put it on the big screen, please.
- Sure. I'll put it on for you.

407
00:32:46,200 --> 00:32:48,840
<i>Promise we'll stay friends forever.</i>

408
00:32:48,920 --> 00:32:51,440
No dating within the group. Ever.

409
00:32:52,320 --> 00:32:53,160
<i>Will you be my boyfriend?</i>

410
00:33:06,240 --> 00:33:07,080
Mochi.

411
00:33:08,560 --> 00:33:09,480
Did you know?

412
00:33:09,560 --> 00:33:13,160
Khobfa's planning a surprise
to ask Rin to be his boyfriend.

413
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:14,840
What?

414
00:33:15,960 --> 00:33:19,400
What did you say, Krit?
Khobfa's asking Rin to be his boyfriend?

415
00:33:20,240 --> 00:33:22,440
But you were hugging Rin the other day.

416
00:33:24,480 --> 00:33:28,520
Oh, I just renewed his domain for him.

417
00:33:29,040 --> 00:33:30,560
We hugged after clearing the air.

418
00:33:32,200 --> 00:33:37,240
Rin even said he was really happy
to see how happy I am with you.

419
00:33:43,840 --> 00:33:46,840
WAIT FOR ME AT THE FACULTY.
I'LL BE THERE SOON.

420
00:33:49,120 --> 00:33:50,680
Why?

421
00:33:50,760 --> 00:33:51,960
Were you jealous?

422
00:33:53,560 --> 00:33:56,480
I moved on from Rin ages ago.

423
00:34:00,960 --> 00:34:03,440
<i>Aren't you the one who's scared?</i>

424
00:34:03,520 --> 00:34:07,920
<i>You're scared that lifting the curse</i>
<i>will mean losing Khobfa, aren't you?</i>

425
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:10,840
<i>You're afraid he'll look at you</i>
<i>and see a stranger, right?</i>

426
00:34:11,520 --> 00:34:13,000
Khobfa, today,

427
00:34:14,360 --> 00:34:15,960
you'll find out the whole truth.

428
00:34:17,760 --> 00:34:19,159
I'll be right back!

429
00:34:25,120 --> 00:34:26,159
Rin!

430
00:34:37,360 --> 00:34:40,520
Would you take someone unlucky
as your boyfriend?

431
00:34:49,080 --> 00:34:51,080
BE MY BOYFRIEND

432
00:34:54,320 --> 00:34:55,840
Will you be my boyfriend, Rin?

433
00:34:57,000 --> 00:35:02,480
- Date him!
- Date him!

434
00:35:02,560 --> 00:35:08,640
- Date him!
- Date him!

435
00:35:08,720 --> 00:35:15,040
- Date him!
- Date him!

436
00:35:20,280 --> 00:35:23,000
Whenever you're ready,
you should tell him.

437
00:35:23,080 --> 00:35:24,480
Take a chance and see what happens.

438
00:35:55,720 --> 00:35:56,920
You're my boyfriend now.

439
00:36:13,920 --> 00:36:15,560
<i>I'm sorry, Khobfa.</i>

440
00:36:15,640 --> 00:36:18,520
<i>I want to make</i>
<i>a few more memories with you.</i>

441
00:36:20,520 --> 00:36:22,520
<i>I'm the heir to a family of mystics.</i>

442
00:36:22,600 --> 00:36:25,800
<i>That day, Krit broke up with me</i>
<i>and started dating Mochi.</i>

443
00:36:25,880 --> 00:36:27,720
<i>I was furious.</i>

444
00:36:27,800 --> 00:36:31,200
<i>So I used the pen to cast a curse on Krit,</i>
<i>wishing him bad luck.</i>

445
00:36:31,280 --> 00:36:35,240
<i>But I found out later</i>
<i>that the pen belonged to Khobfa.</i>

446
00:36:35,320 --> 00:36:39,200
<i>So I cursed Khobfa instead.</i>

447
00:36:39,280 --> 00:36:42,560
<i>I'm the reason</i>
<i>Khobfa keeps having bad luck.</i>

448
00:36:45,240 --> 00:36:46,560
<i>And I let him keep suffering.</i>

449
00:36:46,640 --> 00:36:51,040
<i>If it weren't for that curse,</i>
<i>I wouldn't be here with him today.</i>

450
00:37:25,760 --> 00:37:27,080
Is what you said

451
00:37:28,400 --> 00:37:29,960
in that video true?

452
00:37:30,880 --> 00:37:31,760
Khobfa…

453
00:37:37,080 --> 00:37:37,920
I…

454
00:37:39,240 --> 00:37:40,680
It's my fault.

455
00:37:45,040 --> 00:37:46,560
This is all my fault.

456
00:37:47,320 --> 00:37:49,960
I shouldn't have let things get this far.

457
00:37:55,200 --> 00:37:56,840
I was selfish.

458
00:37:59,160 --> 00:38:01,080
I'm such a fucking asshole.

459
00:38:24,920 --> 00:38:26,200
I'm sorry.

460
00:38:32,920 --> 00:38:36,160
Rin, I…

461
00:39:16,400 --> 00:39:18,440
Please take care of Khobfa for me.

462
00:39:33,280 --> 00:39:35,080
<i>If you make the shot,</i>

463
00:39:35,160 --> 00:39:37,080
<i>I'll let you be my roommate.</i>

464
00:39:38,400 --> 00:39:40,560
<i>Yo, my roommate!</i>

465
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:43,840
- Deal!
- Deal!

466
00:39:56,680 --> 00:39:59,120
<i>Hey, can I leave my dad's pen with you?</i>

467
00:39:59,200 --> 00:40:00,280
Of course.

468
00:40:01,240 --> 00:40:03,480
I'll take the best care
of your dad for you.

469
00:40:03,560 --> 00:40:04,760
I promise.

470
00:40:04,840 --> 00:40:06,640
Good luck.

471
00:40:14,040 --> 00:40:16,360
<i>It's called a dreamcatcher.</i>

472
00:40:16,960 --> 00:40:19,920
<i>You've been having nightmares</i>
<i>and not getting enough sleep.</i>

473
00:40:21,320 --> 00:40:22,880
<i>I just wanted to help you.</i>

474
00:40:33,040 --> 00:40:34,840
<i>I've always worn this bracelet.</i>

475
00:40:35,440 --> 00:40:37,680
<i>I want you to look after it for me.</i>

476
00:40:51,080 --> 00:40:52,520
Take that.

477
00:41:33,280 --> 00:41:36,200
THE CURSER MUST TAKE THE ITEM USED FOR IT,
MAKE A WISH, AND RECITE "FINITO AMORA."

478
00:41:47,560 --> 00:41:49,560
Maybe forgetting me

479
00:41:49,640 --> 00:41:53,920
would be better than having
to hate someone as awful as me.

480
00:41:59,240 --> 00:42:01,240
<i>In a world without me,</i>

481
00:42:01,840 --> 00:42:03,840
you'll finally be happy

482
00:42:04,440 --> 00:42:06,920
and have some real luck in life.

483
00:42:13,800 --> 00:42:16,320
Is what you said in that video true?

484
00:42:17,320 --> 00:42:18,760
Would you take someone unlucky

485
00:42:20,240 --> 00:42:22,000
as your boyfriend?

486
00:42:26,600 --> 00:42:28,800
…AND RECITE "FINITO AMORA."

487
00:42:28,880 --> 00:42:31,600
<i>Finito amora!</i>

488
00:42:45,400 --> 00:42:48,960
<i>Maybe I'm a man who is so unlucky</i>

489
00:42:49,040 --> 00:42:53,160
<i>Like I've been cursed</i>
<i>And everything gets messy</i>

490
00:43:03,640 --> 00:43:04,800
What's wrong?

491
00:43:05,920 --> 00:43:07,760
I feel bad.

492
00:43:07,840 --> 00:43:09,800
You even bought me gold.

493
00:43:11,360 --> 00:43:12,760
Don't feel bad.

494
00:43:13,600 --> 00:43:15,440
You believe in this mystical stuff,
don't you?

495
00:43:15,520 --> 00:43:20,440
People from the past used to believe
gold could break curses.

496
00:43:21,040 --> 00:43:22,640
Now you can finally be lucky.

497
00:43:24,520 --> 00:43:27,080
Why should I be the only lucky one?

498
00:43:28,440 --> 00:43:30,000
It has to be both of us.

499
00:43:30,800 --> 00:43:32,760
We'll both be lucky.

500
00:43:32,840 --> 00:43:33,760
Yeah.

501
00:43:45,920 --> 00:43:47,360
Come on, let's go to bed.

502
00:43:48,920 --> 00:43:51,200
Wait, let go of my hand.

503
00:43:51,280 --> 00:43:52,400
No.

504
00:44:01,480 --> 00:44:02,400
Hey!

505
00:44:06,280 --> 00:44:07,520
Good luck.

506
00:44:20,760 --> 00:44:23,520
<i>I broke the curse.</i>
<i>Khobfa doesn't remember me anymore.</i>

507
00:44:23,600 --> 00:44:24,720
<i>You never know.</i>

508
00:44:24,800 --> 00:44:26,640
<i>He might still remember you.</i>

509
00:44:26,720 --> 00:44:27,760
Watch where you're going.

510
00:44:28,640 --> 00:44:30,160
Khobfa really doesn't remember you.

511
00:44:30,240 --> 00:44:32,600
Do we still have to compete
in the competition?

512
00:44:32,680 --> 00:44:33,880
<i>You have to keep going.</i>

513
00:44:33,960 --> 00:44:36,320
<i>- You have to lead the band to victory.</i>
<i>- You're responsible for it.</i>

514
00:44:36,400 --> 00:44:37,720
<i>Look after our band until the end.</i>

515
00:44:37,800 --> 00:44:38,720
You can't quit.

516
00:44:38,800 --> 00:44:40,440
<i>Why does this feel so familiar?</i>

517
00:44:40,520 --> 00:44:42,320
It's like I've dropped someone off
here before.

518
00:44:43,760 --> 00:44:45,080
We have no idea where Khobfa went.

519
00:44:45,160 --> 00:44:46,120
What?

520
00:44:46,200 --> 00:44:50,680
Let's hear it for Horizon!
